  'uses of frequent patterns': 'Shelf layout, “also bought” lists, spotting fraud, and finding sets of symptoms or genes that turn up together.',
  'recommender systems': 'Programs that choose a few items to show each person out of very many, from what that person and others did before.',
  'similarity': 'A score for how alike two things are. Which score you pick decides what “alike” means: same loans, same proportions, same rare tastes.',
