  'study design': 'Deciding before any data are collected what will be compared with what, and what would count as an answer.',
  'data collection': 'How the values got into the table: who was asked, what was logged, what was left out. Every later step inherits its gaps.',
  // ---- I-14: belief
  'prior, likelihood and posterior': 'The prior is what you believed before the evidence. The likelihood is how well each possibility explains the evidence. The posterior is the updated belief: prior times likelihood, rescaled.',
  'maximum likelihood': 'Choosing the parameter values under which the observed data would have been most probable.',
  'maximum a posteriori': 'Maximum likelihood with a prior: choose the values that are most probable after the evidence is weighed against what was believed before.',
  'naive bayes': 'A classifier that applies Bayes’ rule as if every feature were independent of the others given the class. The assumption is wrong and the method often works anyway.',
